(Bug #69 over a list whose element type IS static. The static path chose its
 comparison from the subject's type alone, so a text subject meant `_str_eq`
 - and a `value` holding a number went into it as a `char*`. The tags decide
 it now: a number never equals a text, so the clause simply does not fire.)

a list called names is ["ann", "-"].

a value called probe is 7.
print each name from names treating probe as "X".

(The same on the replacement side: it fires (both sides are text), and the
 substituted value comes out as the number it is rather than being read as
 a pointer to bytes.)
a value called seven is 7.
print each name from names treating "-" as seven.

(Unchanged: a value that holds text, matched and substituted over the same
 list.)
a value called dash is "-".
a value called anon is "anon".
print each name from names treating dash as anon.
